This folder contains R scripts used for the biomechanical modelling components of this thesis, which includes methodological development and sensitivity analyses described in Chapter 2 and full work flows described in Chapter 3.

Scripts

Chapter 2 Methods Development for Biomechanical Modelling:

  Standardising out-lever calculation by evaluating different approaches.R
  - Compares five approaches for calculating mandibular out-lever lengths: direct (DI), alveolar plane (AV), Frankfort Horizontal plane (FH), and occlusal plane (OC), and an average of the Frankfurt and alveolar measurements (F/A)

  Muscle CSA measurement validation.R
  - Evaluates whether protocols for calculating muscle CSA from adult human CT scans is applicable for an ontogenetic sample.


Chapter 3 Biomechanical Modelling:

  Biomechanical in and out lever calculations 
  - Final script for lever calculations used in this thesis

Data
Input data are not included. Landmark definitions and methodological protocols are described in Chapter 2 of the thesis.
